# game: an example ~/.config/game/config, the house vibes as a skeleton.
# copy it, keep what you like, add what is yours: your author line for
# the bounce, your public root, your word list for the sweep.

# the lint, as described. nothing described is no lint. a repository's
# .game that describes any lint describes all of it, in place of this.
lint width 80
lint rows 25
lint comments
lint print
lint exclaim
lint shout
lint words hyperscaler enterprise-grade blazing-fast load-bearing

# author   Your Name                 the bounce refuses this name in
#                                    the third person
# words    ~/.config/game/sweep.words one word per line the sweep refuses
# exclude  spec-docs/                 left alone by the sweep; repeatable

# a block per project you build, its lines indented under it. the
# repository says which block is its own, with "name" in its .game, and
# holds no remote and no value of its own.
#
# a project with no block here builds and nothing else: there is nowhere
# for a release to go, so there is no release. that is how you try game on
# a repository that is not yours.
#
# project yours
# 	road ../yours-road.git            the dirty remote: every commit
# 	dist git@github.com:you/yours.git the clean one: only game release
# 	set CONTACT you@example.com       a value the repository asked for
